content:
**Term.** On a missed In-Person Appointments visit, a courtesy credit for a long-standing patient is taken off the no-show fee the refund offsets, according to the days from the date the patient's Patient Financial Account was opened to the refund date:

(i) where the financial account was opened **1826 or more** days before the refund date, **15.00** dollars are taken off the no-show fee the refund offsets;

(ii) where it was opened **730 to 1825** days before, **10.00** dollars are taken off;

(iii) where it was opened **fewer than 730** days before, nothing is taken off.

The opening date is the one shown on the Patient Financial Account.

**Across each line (hypothetical accounts).** Open 1826 days on the refund date: paragraph (i), 15.00 dollars. Open 1825 days: paragraph (ii), 10.00 dollars. Open 730 days: paragraph (ii). Open 729 days: paragraph (iii), nothing.
